Debian 13 update (2026-10-01)
----------------------------
See QUALIFICATION-DEBIAN13 for the native amd64/arm64 package qualification.
Ubuntu-only scope statements below describe the initial packaging checkpoint.

Debian/Ubuntu packaging for Qore Oracle
======================================

qore-oracle-module contains the native driver, OracleExtensions source/AOT
module and compiler metadata. The optional documentation package includes both
API references and upstream examples/SQL fixtures. Detached debug symbols are
produced without losing Qore AOT dependency trailers.

Build prerequisites and scope
-----------------------------

Use the packaged Qore 3.0 SDK and Build-Depends from debian/control in an isolated
native environment. This snapshot targets Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 and arm64. Oracle Instant
Client Basic/SDK is a separate proprietary dependency. The recipe under
packaging/instantclient verifies pinned vendor ZIP checksums and builds local
Debian packages without modifying Oracle's binaries. Install those packages in
the builder first. The Oracle client recipe and vendor ZIPs are excluded from
the Qore module source package; the native driver itself is built from source.

Do not upload the proprietary dependency to Launchpad without Canonical's
hosting approval. The module cannot build in the PPA until that dependency is
available in an approved build archive. Public deployment is a separate gate
from local qualification. This package belongs in contrib because it requires
non-free Oracle libraries; no database server is installed by it.

Source and build
----------------

The +ds archive also excludes m4/acx_pthread.m4, an unused legacy Autoconf macro
with no license grant, and cmake/FindOracle.cmake with unspecified BSD terms.
CMake uses the explicitly MIT-licensed FindOracleClient.cmake instead. It accepts
ORACLE_PATH_INCLUDES/ORACLE_PATH_LIB or ORACLE_INSTANT_CLIENT/ORACLE_HOME roots.
CMake does not use Autoconf. From a clean checkout:

    version=3.4.1~git20261004.1+ds
    mkdir -p ../oracle-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-oracle-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' ':!m4/acx_pthread.m4' ':!cmake/FindOracle.cmake' \
        ':!packaging/instantclient' | xz > \
        "../oracle-package-work/qore-oracle-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../oracle-package-work/qore-oracle-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../oracle-package-work
    cp -a debian "../oracle-package-work/qore-oracle-module-$version/"
    cd "../oracle-package-work/qore-oracle-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc into a fresh directory. Build as an unprivileged user with
networking disabled: dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc. -B builds architecture
packages, -A documentation, and DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc omits documentation.
DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc suppresses HTML. Cross builds are rejected because Qore
executes at build time. AOT optimization follows noopt when requested.

Rules derive the minimum Qore runtime and libqore SONAME dependency from the
SDK, while dh_shlibdeps supplies OCI/system-library dependencies. Oracle headers
and libraries are selected explicitly from the packaged SDK, with host Oracle
and Qore environment overrides cleared. No RPATH is added. The runtime package
is not Multi-Arch: same because it requires the native Qore interpreter.

Qualification
-------------

Offline build and installed tests cover driver capabilities and client version,
bind/placeholder descriptors, AQMessage, and OracleExtensions state. The fresh
compiler test exercises native functions/classes and the installed AOT module.
The AOT footer helper has real ELF stripping and error-propagation tests.

Live integration requires a disposable database and QORE_DB_CONNSTR_ORACLE.
Tests create/drop tables, types, procedures and other objects: never use a
production database. Copy tests and the nty SQL fixtures away from the checkout,
explicitly load the freshly built/installed driver, and run suites sequentially.
The named-type suite does not require ssh2 for ordinary tests; its explicit
--reconnect-tests option needs ssh2 and a separately configured remote fixture.
That option can restart a server and is not part of package qualification.

Retain exact dependency versions, source/package hashes, native/live/installed
logs, profiles, byte reproducibility, minimal runtime installation, docs/debug
coinstallation, dpkg -V, purge/reinstall and Lintian evidence. Different Oracle
server/client versions, Debian/Ubuntu releases and architectures need separate
qualification. General release also awaits Qore's ABI freeze and approval.
